# Copy to `client/.env`.
#
# WARNING: Vite inlines every VITE_* variable into the public JS bundle.
# Only non-secret values belong in this file. Secrets live in the repo-root
# .env, which the backend reads and the client never sees.

# Left empty on purpose, and it stays empty in production too. Empty means the
# client calls /api/v1 as a *relative* URL, which the browser resolves against
# whatever origin served the page — the Vite dev server locally, the Cloudflare
# Worker when deployed. Both proxy /api onward, so the browser only ever sees
# one origin and the auth cookies work with no CORS configuration at all.
#
# Do not point this at the deployed API. An absolute URL to another host makes
# every request cross-site, and the cookies are SameSite=lax, which browsers
# refuse to send cross-site. Sign-in would return 200, set a cookie, and every
# request after it would arrive anonymous — with nothing reporting an error.
# The deployed API's origin belongs in the Worker's API_ORIGIN secret instead;
# see client/worker/index.ts.
VITE_API_BASE_URL=

# Same Google OAuth Web client ID as the backend's GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID.
# Public by design — Google client IDs are not secrets.
VITE_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=your-client-id.apps.googleusercontent.com
